/-!
# Singer centralizers for J.2.3

This boundary exports the constructed B-invariant Singer subgroup and
J.2.3(1),(3)–(5): the fixed four-group and cubic commutator, the full
pointwise centralizer product, the marked internal direct product, Sylow
status, order 256 and exact exponent four, all three cubic normalizations,
and the nonabelian Suzuki factor. Its cyclic subgroup of automorphisms acts
on the literal moving factor, and the derived subgroup equals its center
as required by Definition 2.4.13.

`SpecialCore.source_singer_centralizers` retains only the preceding J.2.1
conclusions |Z|=2 and Z≤V and the independent full-commutator assertion
J.2.3(6). Their discharge belongs to the parabolic and SpecialCore assemblies.
The standalone SingerChoice theorems also apply to any specified source choice.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
Lemma J.2.3(1),(3)–(5), printed pp.433–434 (PDF pp.444–445).
-/
